  "notes": {
    "manas-2010:p0033:b002:l030": "сан retained as san, an epic large-number unit; no precise modern headcount invented.",
    "manas-2010:p0033:b002:l032": "Nine san retained, matching the numerical expression rather than replacing it with an unsourced count.",
    "manas-2010:p0034:b002:l003": "Буттап read as measuring by пуд/pood; provisional reading of this witness. No modern-weight conversion.",
    "manas-2010:p0034:b002:l009": "кункор is treated as defective канкор, bloodthirsty one. Bereaved renders тул in the broader context; precise syntax requires review.",
    "manas-2010:p0034:b002:l016": "Contextually retranslated from the complete formula Ордолуу шайык көк жөкөр. Primary 1960 Semetey glossary PDF374 explicitly identifies it as an epithet of Kokand: great/holy/famous city and capital inhabited by many sheikhs. The complete formula, source image and adjacent Kyrgyz verses were individually reviewed; ordinary жөкөр dictionary footwear/retainer senses do not govern this geographic formula. Original raw text, IDs, coordinates and source lineation remain unchanged. Kokand is named immediately before the formula; Bukhara and Samarkand immediately after, in a list of conquered communities.",
    "manas-2010:p0034:b002:l042": "бейпай is an unresolved term; broad torment is used rather than inventing a specific torture method.",
    "manas-2010:p0035:b002:l001": "ажайып is literally wonder/marvel; the referent imposed upon Margalan is unclear and left broad.",
    "manas-2010:p0035:b002:l023": "The three-household cauldron allocation and following single-house clause are preserved, but the exact arrangement is unresolved."
  }
